%description:

Tcp.checksumMode:computed -- the segments carry the checksum of RFC 9293, and a receiver discards a wrong one.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Checksums are declared correct rather than computed, unless
`checksumMode` is "computed" (MUST-2 asks for computed checksums; gap 2 of the TCP
evidence)".

The classes: declared ("declared", the default: the sender writes no checksum and marks the
header as correct) and computed ("computed": the sender computes the checksum of RFC 9293).
The code: Tcp::initialize() puts a TcpChecksumInsertionHook into the IPv4 and IPv6 modules
of the host for "computed"; Tcp::checkChecksum() of the receiver follows the mode that the
header carries, so the parameter of the sender decides whether a receiver can find a wrong
checksum. An invalid value fails at the @enum of the NED. This test separates "computed" from "declared".

Host under test: host1; host1 sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s to host2, which computes no checksum of its
own (the default). The tap replaces the checksum of the first data segment of host1 with its
one's complement and changes nothing else. Observation: level 1, the data segment of host1 carries the
checksum of RFC 9293, and host2 discards the segment whose checksum the tap changed.

%# parameter: Tcp.checksumMode
%# class: computed
%# value: "computed"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.checksumMode
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

// True when the checksum field of the TCP header of the frame holds the value that RFC 9293
// defines for the segment.
static bool hasRfc9293Checksum(const MatchContext& context)
{
    return tcpChecksumField(context.event.packet) == expectedTcpChecksum(context.event.packet);
}

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpChecksumModeComputed")
        .intercept(tap("tap").filterPacket("tcp.destPort == 1000 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .mutate([](Packet *frame) { corruptTcpChecksum(frame); })
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1: replace its checksum with the one's complement"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.destPort == 1000 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
             .filterEvent(hasRfc9293Checksum)
             .describe("the first data segment of host1, with the checksum of RFC 9293")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetDropped")
             .filterPacket("tcp.destPort == 1000")
             .describe("host2 discards the segment whose checksum is wrong")
             .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpChecksumModeComputed compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.checksumMode = "computed"    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpChecksumModeComputed: PASS
